  "canonical": {
    ":question/id": "069b2882-f4a9-589f-a903-4e89d077cd85",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4279",
    ":question/problem": "Suppose, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$. Given that $7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda \\left(3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b} \\right)$ are equal vectors, find the scalar factor $\\lambda$.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that\n\n$$\n7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}= \\dfrac{7}{3} (3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$"
  }
